  "id": "double-insanity",
  "term": "double insanity",
  "definition": "Historically, double insanity meant a form of communicated or shared mental disorder involving two people, such as a pair who come to show the same delusions or hallucinations. In this usage, one person’s disturbed beliefs may influence the other, or both may become affected from a common cause and then intensify each other’s condition through sympathy and imitation.",
